OTHER PEOPLE'S CODE INSIDE THE SHADER
-------------------------------------

The author marks every borrowed helper in the shader with a "License:" comment.
Those comments are kept in main.metal as they were. His CC0 waiver covers his own
work; it does not change the terms of these pieces, which stay as he labelled them:

  hsv2rgb and the HSV2RGB macro   WTFPL, by Sam Hocevar
                                  https://stackoverflow.com/a/17897228/418488
  pmin, flatTorus, cappedTorus,   MIT, by Inigo Quilez
  arc, triIso, rayBox             https://iquilezles.org/

Two more helpers in the original, tanh_approx and hash, are marked there
"License: Unknown". They are NOT in this port: tanh_approx is replaced by the
built-in tanh() and hash by an integer hash written for the port. Both
replacements are offered under CC0-1.0 like the rest.

The MIT terms, for the pieces by Inigo Quilez (the copyright holder named is the
one in the author's comments; the iquilezles.org pages did not load when this was
checked, so the standard MIT text is given here rather than his own notice):

